  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Another round of frost and freeze impacts are expected \ntonight where the growing season continues.\n\nLittle change in the overall synoptic pattern is expected today and\ntonight with strong surface high pressure essentially overhead. The\nhigh will weaken Monday and drift to the south. Slow moderation of\ntemperatures begin today and continue Monday.\n\nFrost Advisories and Freeze Warnings will continue into the morning\nwith clear skies and calm air across the area. We'll see lows in\nthe 30s across most areas with 40s along the shore. Colder temps,\nperhaps some upper 20s, may be observed in the Pine Barrens and\nup across the deeper valleys of North NJ and across into the southern\nPoconos. Like yesterday, we'll evaluate the overnight lows to determine\nif more counties will join the 'Growing Season Ended' list. Check\nout our recent Public Information Statements to see the Current\nstatus of the growing season. \n\nTemperatures today will be a few degrees milder than on Saturday under\nsunny skies. With skies remaining clear tonight, another round of\nfrost is possible tonight into Monday morning. Lows around the region\nwill mainly be in the mid 30s to low 40s. Depending on how Sat night's\nfrost advisories pan out will determine where frost advisories may\nbe warranted for the upcoming night...more details to come in future\nupdates.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Spotty minor tidal flooding may linger today.\n\nWater levels are continuing to decrease in the back bay areas of Ocean\nCounty, NJ and Sussex County, Delaware and no further widespread tidal\nflooding is expected. Spotty minor tidal flooding may linger in the\nback bays though today.",
